Line height `normal` is 1.2 times the font size

0.3.0-beta.4 resolves `line-height: normal` through parley's `NORMAL`,
which is the font's own ascent, descent and line gap. Mail is designed
against the browser references in
crates/postio-test-support/data/reference/, where `normal` came out at
the 1.2 that beta.2 used, and with the font metrics every line is
shorter: a table of three rows in the shipping-notice fixture lost 3px a
row, its page 17px, and fidelity::designed_mail_matches_its_references
failed on height. Keeping 1.2 keeps every reader layout where it was;
the font-metric line height is for a later change that re-blesses the
references on purpose.

Tested by crates/postio-render/tests/render_suite/fidelity.rs.

diff -ruN blitz-dom/src/stylo_to_parley.rs blitz-dom/src/stylo_to_parley.rs
--- blitz-dom/src/stylo_to_parley.rs
+++ blitz-dom/src/stylo_to_parley.rs
@@ -406,7 +406,7 @@
     // Convert font size and line height
     let font_size = font_styles.font_size.used_size.0.px();
     let line_height = match font_styles.line_height {
-        stylo::LineHeight::Normal => parley::LineHeight::NORMAL,
+        stylo::LineHeight::Normal => parley::LineHeight::FontSizeRelative(1.2),
         stylo::LineHeight::Number(num) => parley::LineHeight::FontSizeRelative(num.0),
         stylo::LineHeight::Length(value) => parley::LineHeight::Absolute(value.0.px()),
     };
